<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bead</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as beads</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beads are small decorative objects of glass, stone, shell or metal, pierced for threading, which served widely as trade goods and stores of value. Sub-Saharan beads found at Garamantian sites illustrate the reach of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a>'s trans-Saharan exchange. In southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, imported beads were traded for gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> at coastal centres such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofala">Sofala</a>, linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> empires to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> commerce.</p></div>
